course: dictionary
lesson: 11487
title: Aflame: fire, colour and feeling
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Aflame is a describing word, and it nearly always comes after a verb such as «was» or «set». You say the barn was aflame, or someone set the field aflame. You do not usually put it straight before a noun. Read the words around it: they tell you what is burning, glowing or feeling strong.
explain: «The old barn was set aflame by a spark from the bonfire.» The word fire in the clues, and the spark, tell you aflame means on fire. Ask: what would fit here? Try «on fire» in the sentence instead. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Writers also use aflame for colour. «At sunset the sky was aflame with orange and red.» Nothing is burning there. The colours are so bright they look like flames, so aflame means glowing brightly. Words can paint pictures this way.
explain: Feelings can be aflame too. «Her cheeks were aflame with embarrassment.» Her cheeks were not really on fire. Her face went very red because she felt a strong feeling, so aflame here means full of strong feeling.
fact: Aflame means on fire, burning with flames.
fact: «The bonfire was aflame in the garden» means the fire was burning with flames.
fact: Aflame can mean glowing with bright colour, like «the autumn trees, aflame with gold and red».
fact: Aflame can mean full of a strong feeling, such as anger or excitement: «He was aflame with excitement.»
fact: Aflame usually comes after a verb, as in «be aflame» or «set aflame». Say «the hill was aflame», not «the aflame hill».
fact: Ablaze is a close synonym of aflame when it means on fire, but aflame is the more poetic word.
exercise: «The old barn was set aflame by a spark.» What does aflame mean here? | Painted bright blue | Cold and covered in snow | *On fire, burning with flames | Very quiet and still
exercise: «At sunset the sky was aflame with orange and red.» What does aflame mean in this sentence? | *Glowing brightly with colour, as if burning | Hidden behind a tree | Full of sadness | Dark and cloudy with no colour
exercise: «Her cheeks were aflame with embarrassment.» What does aflame suggest? | *Full of a strong feeling | Cold from the wind | Covered in dirt | Sleepy and tired
test: «The autumn trees stood aflame with gold and red leaves.» What does aflame mean? | *Glowing with bright colour, as if burning | Covered in water | Bare and grey in winter | Very tall and thin
test: «The bonfire was aflame in the garden.» Which word means nearly the same as aflame here? | Cold | Sleepy | *Ablaze | Silver
exam: «He was aflame with excitement as the train pulled in.» What does aflame mean? | Made of wood | *Full of a strong feeling, such as excitement | Asleep and dreaming | Covered in soot from the engine
